error[E0450]: cannot prove that `x` is a `U8` (`x < 256`)
  --> class_type_refined.ck:30:24
   |
30 |         Some x -> Some x
   |                        ^ this must be a `U8`
   = note: counterexample: xs = array.from_list [256]
   = help: make it true first, e.g. with an `if`, or start from a value that is already a `U8`

error[E0262]: type mismatch: expected `Option U8`, found `Option (Take.Item (Array Nat))`
  --> class_type_refined.ck:33:5
   |
33 |     take xs
   |     ^^^^^^^ this expression has type `Option (Take.Item (Array Nat))`, so its `Nat` values aren't known to be `U8`
   = note: a refinement inside a type is never gained from an existing value: that would need a proof about every element
   = help: give the value the type `Option U8` where it is built, so that each part is checked there

class_type_refined.ck: 2 errors, 0 warnings
